The implementation audit also covered correctness, architecture, wire contracts, security and privacy, and verification adequacy.

## Key Findings
- The model check passed: the session file shows provider `onara`, model `cx/gpt-6.1-sol` and thinking level `high`, matching the auditor's pin `onara/cx/gpt-6.1-sol:high`. The trailer's `model_id` matches too.
- The audit trailer passed the trailer check. It is stored verbatim at `.omp/team-config/evidence/csv-total/f2/wave-2/trailer-implementation-audit.md`.
- The record was blocked once. `whole_diff.reason` has to be the text in brackets from `gate.md` (`whole-diff surface reviewed in F2`), not the full `not needed (…)` string. I corrected it and saved the lesson.

## Recommendations
- `validate-openspec-change.mjs --reviewed` still reports `review.md` as stale. Adding fix row 1.3 to `tasks.md` changed the change folder after the planning review. The gate record validates anyway, but `/opsx-apply`'s `--reviewed` check will fail until the planning review is re-run or brought up to date.
- Three QA files are left untracked and unstaged on purpose, because the record doesn't cite them: `wave-1/q9-million.md`, `wave-1/qa-matrix.md` and `wave-2/qa-matrix.md`.
- I didn't lock a separate review worktree: the gate ran in this fixture checkout, which is the only worktree on `feat/csv-total`.

